 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Scale Dominance:** Naive additive accumulation ($H_i += W_i^{(t)}$) allows arbitrarily large evidence increments in one frame, giving large-scale Gaussians disproportionate influence [S1, unofficial]. The tempered update bounds this.
-*   **Closed-Loop Feedback:** In a closed-loop system, rendered label maps drive next-frame association, potentially reinforcing early errors [S1, unofficial]. The tempered update mitigates this by capping the injected mass.
-*   **Injection Bound:** The update satisfies $\eta^{(t)}_i \cdot W^{(t)}_i < \tau$ for $\tau > 0, S_i \ge 0, W^{(t)}_i \ge 0$ [S1, unofficial]. This ensures the total evidence injected by one frame is bounded by $\tau$.
